Indigo needs php (version 8 required), php-xml, and, for the gallery 
example, php-gd. 

The documentation needs the submodules in the indigo/modules directory
to be checked out. Use

	git clone --recurse-submodules

or follow the instructions in your browser.

The directory docs/cache is used for, well, caching and needs to be 
writable by the user the web server runs as.
On most systems it should be sufficient to change the ownership like:

	sudo chown www-data docs/cache

You will be alerted to wrong permissions in your browser window as well.

Otherwise there is no further installation required.
